MID_LGV_Scout_Confirm: Ask {Variable=0} to join you?
MID_LGV_Scout_Terms_Confirm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Terms_Confirm_m01_001: <DLG>It seems {Variable=0} wants something in return.\nHand it over?
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m01_001: Um, hi. Do you have a minute?
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m01_002: I think I could really help you out. If I joined your\nclan, I mean. See, I want to get really strong...
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m01_003: But you probably don't want me, do you? Even if I'd\nbe really useful?
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m02_001: Yay! I can't believe it!
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m02_002: I'm so glad I was brave enough to talk to you!\nThis is really exciting!
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m03_001: I understand... Well, if you ever change your mind,\nlet me know.
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m04_001: Whaaat?! You want to hire me? Why?! Do you think\nI'll be good?
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m04_002: I'm happy, but I don't know if I'm going to be good,\nyou know? It might not be such a great idea. Sorry.
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m05_001: Whaaat?! You want to hire me?
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m05_002: But I'm Cai's friend. I came all the way from Ribeira\nto help him out.
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m05_003: And I don't want to leave Tialla either. Even though\nshe likes...
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m05_004: Anyway, why do you want me to join you?
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m05_005: If you really want to hire me, will you do me a favor?
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m05_006: There's a food I've always wanted to eat... It's called\nRare Ginji. Heard of it?
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m05_007: I guess it bears fruit pretty rarely, so it's super hard\nto come by, but it's supposed to taste amazing.
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m05_008: If you bring me one, I'll think about joining you.\nIt's probably impossible to find though.
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m06_001: Whoa! No way! You found a {Lowercase}Rare Ginji{NormalCase}?!
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m06_002: I bet it was pretty tough to find, huh?
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m06_003: Ughh... I really thought it'd be impossible.
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m06_004: I've been with my friends Cai and Tialla forever.\nBut a deal's a deal, so I'll help you from now on too.
MID_LGV_Scout_Pet_m06_005: So, yeah, I'm Peter, and I'm not too bad at archery.\nI'm looking forward to working with you!
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m01_001: Hey. There's something I want to talk to you about.\nGot a second?
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m01_002: Hello. Pardon me, but there's something I'd love an\nopportunity to speak to you about.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m01_003: I've been interested in you for a little bit. I think I'd\nlearn a lot working with your clan.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m01_004: I believe I'd learn a lot working with your clan, and\nI hope you'd be interested in the possibility.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m01_005: Not to overstep here, but what do you think about\nme joining your crew?
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m01_006: I don't want to seem too forward, but I'm hoping you\nmight see some value in my joining your clan.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m02_001: Great! OK, so that's settled. It's good to be part\nof the team!
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m02_002: Thank you! It feels good to know I can take part in\nyour effort.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m02_003: I'm Ultand Serowain, by the way. I'll do everything\nI can to help you out.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m02_004: Ultand Serowain, at your service!
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m03_001: No worries. Sorry if I came off weird just then. Still, I\nhope you'll keep me in mind.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m03_002: I understand. You have my apologies for bothering\nyou. Please, keep me in mind should the need arise.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m04_001: Heh. You're inviting someone like me to join? Hmm...
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m04_002: Heh. You're inviting someone like me to join? Hmm...
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m04_003: I don't know. I got a lot going on. I don't think I can\nhelp you out right now. Sorry.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m04_004: I apologize, but I have other duties I've promised to\nfulfill. I can't be of help right now.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_001: You want me to join your clan? That's flattering...
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_002: You want me to join your clan? What an honor...
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_003: Except I'm already fighting with the kids of\nRibeira Winds.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_004: Except I'm already fighting with the kids of\nRibeira Winds.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_005: And, listen, I've had a lot of personal stuff going on\nlately, so my head's kind of other places right now.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_006: And I have a lot of other issues in life right now, so\nit's difficult for me to commit.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_007: But if you're serious about needing a fighter, I should\nprobably at least hear you out.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_008: But given that you're in serious need of a fighter, I\nshould probably hear you out.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_009: So here's the thing—I have a problem that needs\nsolving. Interested?
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_010: OK, well, I have a problem that needs solving, and\nI think you have the pull to do it.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_011: Alright, listen. My mom has to work far away,\nand she sent me and my little brothers a package...
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_012: You see, my mother works far away from here, and\nshe sent a package to my younger siblings and me...
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_013: But thieves stole the presents before they reached us.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_014: But thieves stole the presents before they reached us.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_015: The thieves got caught, but by then they'd stashed\neverything in their secret fortress.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_016: The thieves were apprehended, but they had already\nhidden the loot in their secret fortress.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_017: You find the package the thieves stole, and I'll join\nyour clan. Deal?
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m05_018: If you can find the package for me, I'll join your clan.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m06_001: You found the package?! Wow. Thank you so much!
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m06_002: You found the package?! Wow. Thank you so much!
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m06_003: There's clothes, carved wooden toys... Nothing you\ncould call valuable.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m06_004: There's clothes, carved wooden toys... Nothing you\ncould call valuable.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m06_005: But they're from our mom. She's far away, has almost\nno money of her own...and she's still thinking of us.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m06_006: But they're from our mom. She's far away, has almost\nno money of her own...and she's still thinking of us.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m06_007: I owe you—no. My entire family owes you a debt!\nOne I intend to pay.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m06_008: I owe you—no. My entire family owes you a debt!\nOne I intend to pay.
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m06_009: It'll put a strain on my friendship with Cai and the\nothers, but they're good kids. They'll be OK, right?
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m06_010: It will strain my friendship with Cai and the others,\nbut they're good kids. They'll be fine, won't they?
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m06_011: I'm Ultand Serowain, and from now on, I'll fight\nalongside you!
MID_LGV_Scout_Hur_m06_012: Ultand Serowain, yours to command from this day\nforward. I hope to serve you well.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m01_001: You wanna join up with the Infernal Clown, huh?\nSo braaave!
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m01_002: I'm not to be trusted, you know. Might turn around\nand stab you in the back.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m02_001: Heh heh HEH! You want me, you got me!
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m02_002: Let's make a nice big pool of blood—and then go\nswimming in it!
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m03_001: Heh heh... What, scared of me? Good. You should be.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m04_001: Heh heh. You got the right idea, looking to have the\nInfernal Clown on your side.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m04_002: And in return? I won't do anything to you. You ever\nfeel like getting chopped to bits, come on by.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m05_001: You wanna join up with the Infernal Clown, huh?\nMust be pretty brave.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m05_002: Be warned—I'm the fickle type. I might join your\nside today, stab ya in the back tomorrow!
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m05_003: You're that sure, huh? Heh HEH! I like that.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m05_004: But no, Bertrand's got death on him. I smell it. And I\ndon't smell it on you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m05_005: So you ain't winning me over... Well, not unless you\nget a little more death on ya.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m05_006: You hear of the Bale Lacerators? Nasty bunch.\nHoled up in the Dada plains south of the capital.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m05_007: Some villagers went to hunt them down and wound\nup getting themselves carved up something fierce.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m05_008: So! Go give 'em a fight, the sickos. Then maybe I'll\nthink about joining your little crew.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m06_001: Did you beat the Bale Lacerators? Wow.\nYou're better than I thought.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m06_002: If you and your buddies could do that, I guess they\nweren't all that tough.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m06_003: Heh HEH! I smell the blood, but it's not enough.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m07: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m07_001: You really wanna get my attention, you'll need more\ndeath on you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m07_002: Tell ya what. Go to Fort Theed. There's a bandit\ngang there called the Corpse-Gaol Dunanzo.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m07_005: Head to the Valhalla Mine. The bandit gang\nCorpse-Gaol Dunanzo is stationed there.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m07_003: They kidnap people—and their victims never come\nback. So that hideout, it's littered with skeletons.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m07_004: Go and give 'em a fight. Then we'll talk about\njoining up.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m08: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m08_001: Huh? You wiped out Corpse-Gaol Dunanzo?!\nHow'd ya pull that off?!
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m08_002: If you smell like death? Ehhh... I guess you smell\nenough like it.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m08_003: You look all proud of yourself to have beaten 'em.\nBut don't get ahead of yourself, now.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m09: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m09_001: The Underworld Wanderers at Whispering Rock.\nDefeat them and come back to me. 
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m09_002: That bunch is a who's who of scumbags. People call\n'em the couriers of the underworld.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m09_003: If you want to get me on your side—head there.\nYou want to live... Maybe don't.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m010: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m010_001: You're saying you beat the Underworld Wanderers?!\nAnd...it doesn't look like you're lying.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m010_002: {SetColor=Gray}I didn't think that was possible...{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m010_003: {SetColor=Gray}Guess now I have to help out... I feel bad leaving\nBertrand behind.{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m010_004: Heh HEH! You swam a sea of blood, climbed a\nmountain of corpses—even saw the underworld!
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m010_005: And now you'll know true hell, because I'll be there.
MID_LGV_Scout_Max_m010_006: Regretting this yet? Heh heh HEH!
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m01_001: Hey! Got a question. Can I pal around with you and\nyour buddies?
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m01_002: Hey, Cai! Nose to the grind, huh? Heh heh. Always\nworkin' hard—that's why ya beat me!
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m01_003: I've been in the arena for years now, and I wanna\nlearn more about the fighters on the outside.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m01_004: Y'know, it's weird...I kinda wanna help you out.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m01_005: But it's OK if you're not interested... I'll get by.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m01_006: Whaddaya say? Want the Butcher on your side?
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m02_001: Ya sure? Woohoo, thanks!
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m02_002: Bwahaha. I knew you'd say that!
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m02_003: You watch. No matter who we go up against, I'll\npummel 'em into the ground!
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m03_001: Oh, gotcha. OK. Sorry I wasted your time.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m03_002: Makes sense—you're plenty strong on your own.\nWell, gimme a shout if you need anything.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m04_002: Huh? You want me to join your team?
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m04_003: Ooh, don't tell me. You're looking for someone to join\nyour crew?
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m04_004: Bwahaha! You got guts. So I'll let you go home\nwithout any broken bones.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m04_005: Wish I could help ya out, but I gotta stick with\nBertrand. He's my brother!
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m05_001: You want me to join your team, huh? You must be\npretty brave.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m05_002: Cai, always on the move! Are you here to ask for me\nto join your team?
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m05_003: Most people won't even talk to me. They even see\nthe Butcher's face, and they go running.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m05_004: I should probably stick with Bertrand. He's my\nbrother, after all. But I'm rooting for you too...
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m05_005: Since you're so gutsy, I'll make you an offer. See,\nwith all the fightin', I'm starving something fierce.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m05_006: Tell you what. I'll make an offer. See, I've been\nstarving something fierce.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m05_007: The arena food they're feeding me and my buddy\nBertrand just ain't doing the trick.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m05_008: The battles lately have been TOUGH, and the food\nin the arena just ain't doing the trick.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m05_009: Gimme a heap of some tasty meats, and I might\nconsider joining your team! Bwahaha!
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m06_001: Whaaa! You cooked up all that food?
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m06_002: And you're really gonna give it to me?! Dang...\nWell, a promise is a promise.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m06_003: I don't wanna leave Bertrand in the lurch, but I'll\ngive you a hand.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m06_004: I don't wanna leave Bertrand in the lurch, but I\nguess I'll give you a hand, little buddy.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m06_005: You can count on me from now on. I'll pummel the\nother guys into the ground, no matter who they are!
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m07: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m07_001: Bwahaha! Chickened out, huh? I don't blame ya.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m07_002: Aw, makes sense! You guys are plenty strong without\nme anyway. Give me a shout if you need anything.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m08: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m08_001: What? You don't have the meat you promised!\nGet lost before I break something.
MID_LGV_Scout_Gol_m08_002: Bwahaha! You tricked me. That's OK—if you had it,\nI'd be in a real bind.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m01_001: Say! Have you felt a sense that something's missing\nfrom your clan, but you don't know what it is?
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m01_002: I have a favor to ask of Your Majesty. Would you\nallow me to join your clan?
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m01_003: Well, wonder no longer! You need a playwright!\nWhich is to say—me!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m01_004: I have a nose for good subjects, and I must say,\nyou simply reek of promise!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m01_005: It would take many pages to explain fully my value,\nbut in time, I'm certain you will find out!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m01_006: Naturally, I will accompany you in forthcoming\nbattles as well! You'll see me as an asset, trust me.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m02_001: Good choice! No doubt Kalla, the Patron-Huntress, \nwill bless you and your—our!—coterie.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m02_002: Ahaha! I thank you. Henceforth, you will have me\nat your side!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m02_003: I look forward to crossing the horizon with you into\nnew realms of storytelling!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m02_004: I look forward to crossing the horizon with Your\nMajesty into new realms of storytelling!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m03_001: You refuse?! Why, that's a ridiculous decision.\nOne you will sorely regret!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m03_002: So it is not to be? Alas... I cannot help but mourn the\nmasterpiece that could have been...
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m04_001: I am always looking for noteworthy people—\ncharacters who are worth writing about.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m04_002: I am always looking for noteworthy people—\ncharacters who are worth writing about.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m04_003: I'm afraid you seem to fall well short of that.\nProve me wrong, and we can talk.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m04_004: Are you "noteworthy"? Perhaps so...but I don't think \nthere's a book's worth of material in your story.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m05_001: So I've piqued your interest, mm? From my\nperspective, it is YOU doing all the piquing!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m05_002: So I've piqued your interest, mm? From my\nperspective, it is YOU doing all the piquing!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m05_003: You have a unique quality... Yes. The unmistakable\nwhiff of greatness.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m05_004: You have a unique quality... Yes. The unmistakable\nwhiff of greatness.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m05_005: As a master auteur, I cannot help but desire to follow\nthat smell—tell your story!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m05_006: As a master auteur, I cannot help but desire to follow\nthat smell—tell your story!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m05_007: Though I'm doing research for The Rise of the\nWhite-Maned Demon, I could make time to join you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m05_008: Though I'm doing research for The Rise of the\nWhite-Maned Demon, I could make time to join you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m05_009: That said...a writer of my talents does not work\nfor free. You would need to cover my expenses.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m05_010: That said...a writer of my talents does not work\nfor free. You would need to cover my expenses.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m06_001: Good choice! No doubt Kalla, the Patron-Huntress, \nwill bless you and your—our!—coterie.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m06_002: Ahaha! I thank you. Henceforth, you will have me\nat your side!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m06_003: I look forward to crossing the horizon with you into\nnew realms of storytelling!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m06_004: I look forward to crossing the horizon with Your\nMajesty into new realms of storytelling!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m07: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m07_001: You refuse? A pity. You're letting go of the chance\nto birth a masterpiece.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m07_002: You refuse? That's regrettable... I fear you're giving\nup the chance to birth a masterpiece.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m08: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m08_001: Oh, this is awkward. You lack the money I require.\nWell, I won't run—come back when you have it.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dan_m08_002: It seems you don't have enough... Well, I can wait.\nPlease come back when you have it.
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m01_001: Hey, quick question. Can I join up with you?
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m01_002: I want to fight and get stronger. Sweetie loves strong\npeople best!
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m01_003: If I'm with you, I should be able to hone my skills.\nPromise I won't let you down!
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m02_001: Really? Thanks! Like I said, I'm ready to work!
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m02_002: I may look like I grew up in a fishing village, because\nI did. But I'm plenty strong AND can catch dinner!
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m03_001: Come on! I really do want to get stronger, and I'll\ngive it my all. I'm here if you need me!
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m04_001: Uh, what? Join up with you? Me...in your clan?
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m04_002: Sorry, I'm devoted to my Sweetie, and that's that.\nI won't be lured away.
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m05_001: Will I join your clan? Are you serious?
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m05_002: I'm devoted to Sweetie—Dietrich, I mean. Sorry, but\nyou can't talk me into it.
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m05_003: Hmm. You want me to join you and you won't take\nno for an answer? I'm a little flattered, I'll admit.
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m05_004: I see. Well, I don't know if this'll work out or not, but\nyou probably deserve a chance.
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m05_005: My hometown is a fishing village called Fina.\nThere's not much there, but it's a good place.
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m05_006: Right nearby, you'll find Cape Damasen, where\nthere's a colony of aggressive sea beasts.
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m05_007: Nobody from my village will go near the place, so\nyou'd be doing them a favor if you finished 'em off.
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m05_008: You don't look like much, but if you can get it done,\nI'll join up. I mean, how could I say no?
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m06_001: You got rid of those sea beasts? I didn't expect much,\nbut...you're pretty good, aren't you?
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m06_002: Seems more and more of them have been making\nthe cape their stomping grounds lately.
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m06_003: I was worried about my mom back in Fina, but I\nguess I don't have to anymore!
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m06_004: Well, you've made your point. You're strong, and you\ndid what it takes to show me that.
MID_LGV_Scout_Esm_m06_005: My heart is Sweetie's and only Sweetie's, but I'm\nhappy to lend you a hand in battle. You earned it!
MID_LGV_Scout_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Sim_m01_001: Hey there, something you wanna ask? If there's a\nfight coming, you can count me in.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sim_m01_002: The battlefield proves that whether you win or lose is\nalways up to you. That's why I love it so much.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sim_m01_003: So how about it? As long as the work's not too dirty,\nI'll take any job you got.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sim_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Sim_m02_001: Alright, lead the way. From now on, you can rest\neasy knowing I'll have your back.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sim_m02_002: Let's go crack some skulls!
MID_LGV_Scout_Sim_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Sim_m03_001: Oh... Well, I'll keep my schedule open just in case.\nIf you're ever short on numbers, just gimme a shout.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sim_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Sim_m04_001: I mean, sure, working for Talimun doesn't mean I\nbelong to the guy...
MID_LGV_Scout_Sim_m04_002: But as you are now? Sorry, but sticking with the boss\njust seems more exciting. Maybe some other time.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sim_m04_003: But as you are now? Sticking with the boss just\nseems more exciting. Maybe another time, Majesty.
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m01_001: Here I was, wondering what you'd say, and turns out\nit's "join up with me."
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m01_002: Well, Talimun may have hired me, but that doesn't\nmean I belong to Vandahl Trading.
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m01_003: Y'know, the job's been too cushy lately. Maybe riding\nwith you will give me the rush I'm looking for.
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m01_004: But a clean switch would be kinda boring, don'tcha\nthink? How 'bout we have a little competition?
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m01_005: I'll flip a coin, and you guess it—heads or tails.
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m01_006: Not for free, of course. One go will cost you...five\nhundred gold. You game?
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m01_007: <ICA>Tell him you accept.
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m01_008: <ICB>Tell him you're not interested.
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m02_001: Great! Then you're on!
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m02_002: Alright, ready? And...GO! Which is it, heads or tails?
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m02_003: <ICA>Pick heads!
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m02_004: <ICB>Pick tails!
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m02_005: <ACA>Ahh... Man, that's rough. Sorry, but it's tails. I'll be\nkeeping your five hundred gold.
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m02_006: <ACA>You can play as much as you want. No need to be\nshy about it. Seriously... I don't mind the money.
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m02_007: <ACB>Hell yeah! It's Tails! Looks like you win.
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m02_008: <ACB>Ha! You've either got impressive luck or impressive\neyes! Regardless, consider me on your roster.
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m02_009: <ACB>As long as the work doesn't get too dirty, I'll take\ndown whoever or...whatever you need.
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m02_010: <ACB>The more challenging, the better—whatever gets the\nheart pumping.
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m02_011: <ACB>Let me introduce myself again. I'm Simon. Simon\nClairmont. I look forward to having your back!
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_Sim_m03_001: What, you getting cold feet? Come find me if you\nchange your mind.
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_NoMoney_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Negotiation_SP_NoMoney_Sim_m01_001: Ah, looks like you don't have enough gold, friend.\nFeel free to come back when you have more.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m01_001: Hey! You won't believe the intel I just heard. Hire me\non, and I'll tell you! C'mon, I'll even work for free!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m01_002: Hey, I have some intel you might want to know.\nHire me on, and it's yours! I'll even work for free!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m01_003: Talimun asked me to help out anyone who looks\nlike they could use a hand from Vandahl Trading!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m01_004: Talimun asked me to help out anyone who looks\nlike they could use a hand from Vandahl Trading!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m02_001: Then it's settled! With skills like mine, you can leave\nall the tough guys to me.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m02_002: Great! It'll be an honor to work with you. I'm as\nsharp as they come, so count on me!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m02_003: Because I'm the daughter of General Senghor, leader\nof the Eleventh Division of the imperial military!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m02_004: Because I'm the daughter of General Senghor, leader\nof the Eleventh Division of the imperial military!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m03_001: H-hey, wait a sec! I did say "free," didn't I? You're\nskipping out on an amazing deal, you know?!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m03_002: B-but you'd be getting me for free... That's a pretty\nsweet deal, you know.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m04_001: Huh?! You want to recruit me?
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m04_002: WHAAAA?! Really?! You want to recruit me?
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m04_003: I'd love to, but I still have responsibilities at the\nVandahl Trading Company... Sorry!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m04_004: I'm so honored, but I still have responsibilities at\nVandahl Trading... I'm sorry.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_001: Interested in any of our merch... Oh, you're looking\nfor me?!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_002: Can I interest you in any of our merchandise?\nOh, you're interested in...me?!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_003: Sorry, but right now I'm working for Talimun at\nVandahl Trading...
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_004: I'm sorry, but at the moment, I'm working for\nTalimun at the Vandahl Trading Company.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_005: And I can't say this too loudly, but there's still a few\nthings my father has asked me to do here as well.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_006: And I can't say this too loudly, but there's still a few\nthings my father has asked me to do here as well.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_007: Between me trying to do a good job and my father's\nrequests, it's already kind of a lot...
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_008: Between me trying to do a good job and my father's\nrequests, it's already kind of a lot...
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_009: But I feel like you can keep a secret. Maybe you\nwouldn't mind helping me?
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_010: But I trust you can keep a secret. Maybe... Would you\nmind helping me?
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_011: My father's a general of the Dagdan military, with a\npretty big grudge against Talimun.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_012: My father is a general of the Dagdan military, with a\npretty big grudge against Talimun.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_013: So I've been feeding him intel about the company,\nbut he's interested in our most recent branch.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_014: So I've been feeding him intel about the company,\nbut he's interested in our most recent branch.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_015: I know goods are being sent to the new branch from\nour branch in the Callianeira Port.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_016: I know goods are being sent to the new branch from\nour branch in the Callianeira Port.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_017: But I need someone to visit the port and report back\nany intel they hear about the new branch.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_018: But I need someone to visit the port and report back\nany intel they hear about the new branch.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_019: If you do this for me, I'll know I can trust you.\nWhen it's over, we can talk about me joining you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m05_020: If you do this for me, I'll know I can trust you.\nWhen it's over, we can talk about me joining you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m06_001: You did it! My father should be pretty happy with\nthis intel.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m06_002: You did it! My father should be pretty happy with\nthis intel.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m06_003: You know, it'd be such a big help if you could keep\nassisting me in this... Hey, how about this...
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m06_004: It would mean a lot if you could keep assisting me in\nthis... Hey, here's an idea...
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m06_005: I'll make sure the Vandahl Trading Company makes\nyou our valued VIP customers.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m06_006: I'll make sure the Vandahl Trading Company makes\nyou our valued VIP customers.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m06_007: That way, there's a business justification for me\nhelping you out while staying with the company.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m06_008: That way, there's a business justification for me\nhelping you out while staying with the company.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m06_009: In exchange, you'll work with me when I need.\nIf that sounds good, it's a deal!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m06_010: In exchange, you'll work with me when I need.\nIf that sounds good, it's a deal!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m06_011: I may look soft and sweet, but I'm a soldier's\ndaughter, trained to fight! You can count on me!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lou_m06_012: I may look soft and sweet, but I'm a soldier's\ndaughter, trained to fight! You can count on me!
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m01_001: Oh... Excuse me. If you have time, there's something\nI've been meaning to ask you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m01_002: Would you consider having me by your side? I made\nan error while cleaning the company storehouse.
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m01_003: I threw away a priceless urn, thinking it was garbage.\nI was so careless... I need to learn to be...better.
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m02_001: Really?! Th-thank you so much...
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m02_002: My healing is unparalleled. I can mend any manner\nof wound or ailment.
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m03_001: Of course... My apologies. If you are ever in need of a\nhealer, please come find me...
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m04_001: Oh, it's you! You weren't trying to get my attention\nwere you?
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m04_002: I would not even entertain leaving Talimun's side.\nPlease...be on your way.
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m05_001: Hm? Did you want to ask me something? Thank you\nfor your interest, but please, try elsewhere...
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m05_002: I want to remain by Talimun's side but don't have\nthe strength to do so...
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m05_003: The truth is I have no memory of my past. Knowing\nthat, I must work harder than most.
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m05_004: I know! Perhaps you could train me in secret?\nIf so, then I accept your invitation.
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m05_005: I'll tell Talimun that this is work-related. Could you\noffer compensation in case he gets curious?
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m06_001: Really?! Th-thank you so much...
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m06_002: My healing is unparalleled. If any of your party fall\ninjured, know they will be safe in my hands.
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m07: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m07_001: Yes, of course... My apologies. If you change your\nmind, please come find me...
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m08: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Fia_m08_001: My apologies, but it seems you don't have it...\nCruel of you to get my expectations up...
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m01_001: Hey, you're pretty strong, yeah? Can I join up\nwith you?
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m01_002: You look my age, but you're kinda strong, right?
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m01_003: I was trained up by temple soldiers! I can do\nthings! Give me a chance!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m01_004: I was trained by temple soldiers! Let me join up\nwith you!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m02_001: Ha, thanks! Now I can get even stronger!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m03_001: What? You gotta be kidding me. Come on!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m04_001: Look, did you really think I'd tag along with just\nanyone because they asked?
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m04_002: You know, I've seen my fair share of bad stuff.\nI know I'm still young, but I'm not a fool.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m04_003: I've been through some stuff and gotten burned.\nI know we're both young, but I'm not a fool.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m05_001: Hey, so... Word is you're pretty strong. People all\nover are talking about you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m05_002: So you know that people are talking about you, right?\nWord is you're really strong!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m05_003: So YOU came to invite me? Ha! Guess I've got\nsomething to offer!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m05_004: So you really came to invite me? Ha! Guess I've\ngot something to offer!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m05_005: I was taught how to use a blade from someone I\nknow called Ozin. But I can get even better!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m05_006: I'm working for Orchel now, but if I don't have to\nquit helping the priest lady, I can help you too.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m05_007: But I don't trust just anybody. How about you give\nme this? It's a fair deal!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m06_001: Oh! Great! I'm looking forward to working with you!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m06_002: With the blade skills I learned from Ozin, I'll cut\ndown all your enemies!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m07: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m07_001: What? If you were gonna say no, why'd we even\ntalk in the first place?
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m08: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m08_001: Hey! That's NOT what I asked for! What, you think\nthat I'm just a dumb kid or something?!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lor_m08_002: Hey, that's NOT what I wanted! You messing with\nme or something? You'd better not be!
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m01_001: What? Are you interested in me fighting as part\nof your group?
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m01_002: Could it be...that you know who I am? Ah, never\nmind me. Just a passing thought.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m01_003: I'm merely a traveler passing through the area.\nStill, you'd like me to join you?
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m02_001: Well, I never mind providing assistance to those\nyounger than I when asked for help.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m02_002: I agree and gladly so. Let's work together from\nnow on.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m03_001: I see. Then my travels continue.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m04_001: Hmm, you're eager to recruit me? I didn't see this\ncoming, but I'm not opposed to the idea.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m04_002: I don't have time for it presently. You'd be better off\nfinding someone more suited for it right now.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m05_001: You're asking me to join your clan? I would oblige,\nbut it's not quite that easy.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m05_002: I'm supporting Orchel currently, and I also have\nsome business across this land.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m05_003: Hmm... But I sense you'd like me to reconsider.\nYou must think highly of me.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m05_004: Well then, perhaps you can do me a favor. It's rather\nimportant. So please, hear me out.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m05_005: Now, this must stay between us. I haven't even told\nOrchel and the others about it.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m05_006: I have skill in smithing, and not long ago, I forged\nweapons for some defenseless villagers.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m05_007: The weapons were simple but sufficient. Still, later,\nthieves ravaged that poor village.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m05_008: Their leader now carries one of those weapons and\nuses it during their wicked travels. Quite vexing.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m05_009: I'd like you to bring justice to those thieves—and\nbury my weapon where you find those rogues.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m05_010: I know of their whereabouts. I'll consider your\nrequest if you can help me with this matter.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m06_001: Ah, so you defeated the thieves? Thank you. I'm\nsure it brought peace to the villagers' souls.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m06_002: They were good people. It's truly a shame. I have\nso much regret about all of this.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m06_003: If I had only given the villagers stronger weapons,\ncould they have survived?
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m06_004: Or would the thieves have wound up getting stronger\nweapons, leading to worse violence?
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m06_005: Ah, forgive me. I didn't mean to trouble your mind\nwith such thoughts. I must feel at ease with you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Set_m06_006: I don't want to neglect Orchel, but I will lend you\nmy support as well. So, you can count on me.
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m01_001: Oh... You must want me to join you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m01_002: I sense that the others here don't think badly of you...
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m01_003: Fine then. I'll fight for you as long as it doesn't\ninterfere with my responsibilities.
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m02_001: Very well. I'll lend you my strength.
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m02_002: The spirits seem...pleased. Yes, a good sign.
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m03_001: How changeable of you. That's alright with me.
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m04_001: Most people I meet shy away from me. Yet here\nyou are, asking me to join you. How strange.
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m04_002: But I'd advise you to stay away. Those who come\ntoo close find only misery with me. Farewell.
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m05_001: You want me to join you? How strange. Most\npeople find me a bit frightening.
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m05_002: I serve Credna's temple as a vulkan, tasked at\npresent with protecting Lead Priest Orchel.
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m05_003: But, you here, now... Interesting. I sense that the\nothers here don't think badly of you...
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m05_004: I find myself curious. Though I won't abandon\nOrchel, I will lend you some of my support.
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m05_005: As for a contract... I need no payment, but if that's\nwhat's normal, how about this?
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m06_001: So we have a deal. As of today, you will find me\nalongside you, fighting.
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m06_002: Oh, you all think so... Yes, the spirits are happy.\nThis must be a good sign.
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m07: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m07_001: How changeable of you. That's alright with me.
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m08: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Nin_m08_001: That's not what I requested. Ensure that you\nunderstand what I asked of you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m01_001: Yeah? Got something you wanna ask me?
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m01_002: Ask, then. Queen Theodora said I could do whatever\nas long as it doesn't interfere with my military duties.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m01_003: My services aren't cheap, but you get what you\npay for.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m02_001: Alrighty. Looks like I'll be working with you from\nnow on.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m02_002: Pay me fairly, and I guarantee you'll be happy with\nmy work.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m03_001: So much for negotiations. Damn...and here I'd hoped\nthis could be a new income source for me.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m04_001: Y'know, I don't get too many offers like this, but it's\nkinda nice.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m04_002: Too bad I'm in Queen Theodora's service. So let's\nforget the whole thing. Sorry!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m05_001: Oh, you want me to join you? Because I'm good with\na bow? Aw, thanks.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m05_002: But I'm on Queen Theodora's payroll right now.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m05_003: That said...I never turn down a payday. So I don't\nmind helping you out on the side.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m05_004: What can you offer me as a down payment? I'll let\nyou know now, I don't work cheap.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m06_001: Uh, seriously? That much? Sweet! I guess it really\ndoesn't hurt to ask.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m06_002: I'll work as hard as you pay me for. And for that\nmuch, I'll work pretty hard!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m07: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m07_001: Huh? Not even gonna haggle? Damn...I was hoping\nthis would be a new source of income.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m08: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lil_m08_001: Hey, this isn't enough! If you couldn't afford me,\nyou should've just said so.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m01_001: Pardon me! I have a question, which shouldn't take\nup much of your time. What do you say?
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m01_002: Her Majesty directed me to observe tactics from\noutside of Saramis to broaden my perspective.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m01_003: Would you take me on as an ally? Fighting alongside\nyou seems like an excellent learning opportunity.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m02_001: So you'll have me?! Thank you!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m02_002: Let us aid each other as allies!
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m03_001: You won't, hm? Well, minds can change. I hope you'll\nconsider it and return to me another day.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m04_001: You want my strength? Hah! I'm honored.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m04_002: But I am a proud warrior of Saramis. I'm reluctant to\nwield this spear for anyone other than my queen.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m05_001: You want me to fight for you? Ordinarily, I wouldn't\neven consider it. However...
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m05_002: I've thought for some time that I ought to broaden\nmy perspective for the sake of Saramis, my home.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m05_003: I will always be Queen Theodora's retainer, but by\nher leave, I'd be willing to work with you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m05_004: But I would like some evidence of your good faith.\nFor example, can you offer something like this?
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m06_001: Oh! Thank you for agreeing so readily.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m06_002: From now on, my spear is yours. Let us aid\none another.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m07: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m07_001: Too steep? That's a shame. If you change your mind,\nseek me out again.
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m08: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Lys_m08_001: You don't actually have it, do you? This is\nunfortunate... I wanted to believe in you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m01_001: You wish to have me as your ally? Hmmm. Normally,\nI decline propositions from men.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m01_002: Oho! You wish to have me by your side,\nbeautiful one?
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m01_003: Oho! You wish to have me by your side,\nmy beautiful queen?
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m01_004: But like the wind, I am ever-changing. Perhaps I may\nfind some amusement down this path.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m01_005: I would never dream of turning down a request from\nsuch an enchanting specimen.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m01_006: I would never dream of turning down a request from\nsuch an enchanting woman.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m01_007: If you say you want me by your side in battle,\nI will accept.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m01_008: After all, through the trials of battle, who knows?\nA passionate love may bloom.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m01_009: After all, through the trials of battle, who knows?\nA passionate love may bloom.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m02_001: Very well. You may rest easy now, knowing that you\nhave me by your side.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m02_002: When battle rings out, call upon me. I swear on my\ngoddess that I will strike our foes like a fiery wind.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m02_003: When battle rings out, call upon me. I swear on my\ngoddess that I will strike our foes like a fiery wind.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m02_004: Do not think me a mere bard. Like a fiery wind,\nI will strike our foes.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m02_005: Of course, you're welcome to call upon me outside\nbattle as well...
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m02_006: Naturally, you're welcome to call upon me outside\nbattle as well...
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m03_001: I see—evidently, someone can't tell which way the\nwind blows. Were you purposefully wasting my time?
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m03_002: Aha! Pulling me in, only to push me away. Well,\nI don't mind being teased.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m03_003: Aha! Pulling me in, only to push me away. Well,\nI do not mind being teased.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m04_001: Oh? You wish to proposition me, hm? You seek the\nFiery Wind upon which victory floats.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m04_002: Oh, to receive a proposition from a lady such as you!\nHoping to hear a song of love in your bedroom, hm?
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m04_003: But the wind is a fickle thing, and it does not blow in\nyour direction. Would you leave?
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m04_004: But the wind is a fickle thing, and it does not blow in\nyour direction at the moment. Apologies.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_001: Oh? I wondered what this might be about.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_010: Well, well! I wondered why such a beauty might\napproach. You're propositioning me.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_018: Well, well! I wondered why such a beauty might\napproach. You're propositioning me.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_002: As much as I would enjoy traveling with you, right\nnow I am the wind behind Miss Leda's sails.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_012: Sadly for you, I still hew tightly to the beautiful rose\nthat is Miss Leda.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_019: Sadly for you, I still hew tightly to the beautiful rose\nthat is Miss Leda.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_003: So, although I appreciate the proposition,\nI must decline.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_011: So, although I am charmed by your overture, I must\nrespectfully decline.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_020: So, although I am charmed by your overture, I must\nrespectfully decline.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_004: Hmm. You're not deterred? Well, far be it from me to\nfend off such a fervent pursuer, regardless of sex...
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_013: Hmm. You're not deterred? Well, far be it from me to\nfend off such a fervent pursuer.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_021: Hmm. You're not deterred? Well, far be it from me to\nfend off such a fervent pursuer.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_005: In recognition of your passionate feelings, I shall\noffer one opportunity to win my allegiance.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_014: In recognition of your passionate feelings, I shall\noffer one opportunity to win my allegiance.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_022: In recognition of your passionate feelings, I shall\noffer one opportunity to win my allegiance.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_006: There is a poet who has shaped my very heart.\nLet us call him the legendary poet.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_015: There is a poet who has shaped my very heart.\nLet us call him the legendary poet.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_023: There is a poet who has shaped my very heart.\nLet us call him the legendary poet.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_007: Recently I heard a rumor of a stone monument into\nwhich one of his works is engraved.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_016: Recently I heard a rumor of a stone monument into\nwhich one of his works is engraved.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_024: Recently I heard a rumor of a stone monument into\nwhich one of his works is engraved.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_008: If there's truth in this claim, then I'd very much like\nto see that verse. Find it, and make a copy of it for me.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_009: Do so, and I will consider becoming your ally.\nThere—a task for you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_017: Do so, and I will consider becoming your ally.\nThere—a task for you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m05_025: Do so, and I will consider becoming your ally.\nThere—a task for you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m06_001: Ohhh... The depth and breadth of emotion! The more\nI read it, the more it plucks at my heartstrings.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m06_002: This is indeed the work of my legendary poet.\nWell done. You have my gratitude.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m06_007: This is indeed the work of my legendary poet.\nYou found it.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m06_011: This is indeed the work of my legendary poet.\nYou found it.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m06_003: I expected you to abandon this impossible mission.\nYou have my gratitude for seeing it through.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m06_008: I expected you to abandon this impossible mission...\nI'm grateful you saw it through.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m06_012: I expected you to abandon this impossible mission...\nI'm grateful you saw it through.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m06_004: I will continue watching over Miss Leda, as my\ngoddess wishes.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m06_005: But—as for my own wishes—now I will endeavor\nto protect you too.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m06_009: But—as for my own wishes—please, allow me to\nprotect you too.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m06_013: But—as for my own wishes—please, allow me to\nprotect you too.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m06_006: Turn to me when you need help. Call my name,\nand I'll be there, swift as a gale.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m06_010: Never forget the name Sirocco. Call my name, and I'll\nbe there, swift as a gale.
MID_LGV_Scout_Sci_m06_014: Never forget the name Sirocco. Call my name, and I'll\nbe there, swift as a gale.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m01_001: What's going on? You want me to be your ally?
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m01_002: What's the matter? You want me to be your ally?
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m01_003: Hehe. I'm glad you think I'm worth recruiting.\nEveryone treats me like a kid.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m01_004: I'm glad you think I'm worth recruiting. Everyone\ntreats me like a kid.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m02_001: OK, let's do it! I won't let you down!
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m02_002: Alright, let's do it! I won't let you down.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m03_001: Huh? Oh, guess I got ahead of myself... That's\nembarrassing.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m03_002: Huh? I must have gotten ahead of myself... That's\nembarrassing.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m04_001: Let me guess. You want me to be your ally?
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m04_002: Let me guess. You'd like for me to be your ally?
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m04_003: Hm. I hate to be rude, but that's a lot to ask. I barely\nknow you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m04_004: I'm sorry, but I don't think that's a good idea. I hardly\nknow you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m05_001: You want me to be your ally? Is that because I know\nso much about medicinal herbs?
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m05_002: You would like me to be your ally? Is that because\nI know so much about medicinal herbs?
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m05_003: Hehe. Most people treat me like a kid, so it's nice to\nhear you say that.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m05_004: Hehe. Most people treat me like a kid, so it's nice to\nhear you say that.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m05_005: I'm working with Leda, but maaaybe I can help you\nout too.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m05_006: I'm working with Leda, but I would consider helping\nyou out too.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m05_007: But I won't become your ally just like that. Maybe if\nyou find me something I need, I'll think about it.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m05_008: But I won't become your ally just like that. Maybe if\nyou find me something I need, I'll consider it.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m06_001: You got it! I've been wanting this forever. And you're\nreally gonna give it to me? Thanks!
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m06_002: You got it! I've been wanting this forever. And you're\nreally gonna give it to me? Thanks!
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m06_003: This proves I can trust you. Alright, that settles it.\nI'm looking forward to working together!
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m06_004: Guess this proves I can trust you. Alright, that\nsettles it. Looking forward to working together!
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m07: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m07_001: Whaaa? You're not gonna give it to me? Fine.\nThen I won't help you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m07_002: Whaaa? You're not gonna give it to me? Then I'm\nsorry, but I won't help you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m08: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m08_001: Huh? You don't have it. Well, maybe another time.
MID_LGV_Scout_Moo_m08_002: Huh? You don't have it. Fine, then don't worry\nabout it... See you another time.
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m01_001: Hey, got any work that needs doing?
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m01_002: I made my name as a mercenary, and I'm not afraid\nof tough jobs.
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m01_003: I've managed to earn some coin from it, and I'd like\nto earn some more. What do you say?
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m02_001: Great. We're under contract. I'll work hard for my\npay—just you watch.
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m02_002: As long as you're honorable, I'll stick with you.\nRest easy!
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m03_001: Changed your mind, did you? Just find me again if\nyou change it back.
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m04_001: People from across the city seek me out and ask for\nmy help. You're no different.
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m04_002: Unfortunately for you, there's a person I owe a favor,\nso find somebody else.
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m05_001: I wonder what it is that we might talk about. Let me\nguess—you want me to join you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m05_002: I used to be a mercenary, so I'm used to people\ncoming to me.
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m05_003: But Dietrich helped me out when I needed it. I can't\njust leave him in the lurch.
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m05_004: I am trying to save money though... So here's what\nwe'll do. If you make it worth my while, I'll help you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m06_001: Great. We're under contract. I look forward to\nworking with you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m06_002: As long as you're honorable, I'll stick with you.\nRest easy!
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m07: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m07_001: Changed your mind, did you? Just find me again if\nyou change it back.
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m08: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Mic_m08_001: Seriously? That isn't enough. Business is business.\nIt's a hard lesson, but you need to learn it sometime.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m01_001: Mm, yes? Enchanted, are you?
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m01_002: Is something the matter...or were you just enchanted\nby me?
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m01_003: You possess a keen aesthetic eye—and you're not\nwanting for ability, from what I hear.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m01_004: You possess a keen aesthetic eye, Queen Theodora—\nand you're not wanting for ability, from what I hear.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m01_005: I would assent to gracing your battles with\nmy beauty.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m01_006: Would you permit me to join you in the dance of\ncombat, Your Majesty?
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m02_001: Let us be off, then! I look forward to sharing the\nstage with an appreciator of beauty.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m02_002: Very well. Then I shall blossom in full glory for you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m02_003: Prepare to bear witness to the elegance of the Blue\nRose of Caelus!
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m02_004: All will tremble with awe before the elegance of\nYour Majesty and the Blue Rose of Caelus!
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m03_001: I see. Well, it is of no consequence. I will be no less\nbeautiful when you face me as an enemy!
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m03_002: You wish to achieve full, glorious bloom on your\nown? I understand the feeling well.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m04_001: Ah, yes, when witnessing one such as I, it's natural\nthat you would ask me. How could you not?
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m04_002: But—and I beg your pardon—it seems an ill fit.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m04_003: But I'm afraid we are not suited for one another, so I\nmust humbly decline.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m05_001: What is it? Enchanted, were you?
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m05_002: Is something the matter? Or were you simply\nenchanted by me?
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m05_003: To be expected. I have been recognized by Kalla the\nPatron-Huntress as the Blue Rose of Caelus.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m05_004: Sometimes I chafe at all the attention—propositions\nfrom this person and that, every single day!
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m05_005: Rather than replying individually, which would be\ntaxing, I say the same thing to all of them.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m05_006: "Bring me all the items I desire, and I shall be yours."
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m05_007: Will you take me up on this offer? Then listen\nclosely.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m05_008: Are you interested in taking me up on this offer?\nThen please, listen closely.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m05_009: While coffee is the more popular beverage in Dagda,\nI myself prefer tea.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m05_010: To win my heart, you must first bring me some tea of\nthe highest quality.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m05_011: What I desire is the rare brew known as Scarlet\nFiredrops. Ohoho... I will be waiting!
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m06_001: You've brought me my tea already? Mhm, yes, this is\nthe brew I requested.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m06_002: Well done. But you are far from the first to acquire it.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m06_003: The items will be more and more difficult to acquire\ngoing forward. Brace yourself and listen well!
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m06_004: The items will be more and more difficult to acquire\ngoing forward. Steel yourself and listen well!
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m07: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m07_001: Flowers are the pinnacle of beauty and elegance.\nI have admired many in my life.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m07_002: But the most glorious are often those that grow in the\nharshest climes. They possess a divine solemnity.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m07_003: Bring me the {Lowercase}Aurum Rose{NormalCase}, a golden rose that\nendures and blooms amid hot desert sands.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m07_005: Bring me the {Lowercase}Aurum Rose{NormalCase}, a golden rose that\nendures and blooms amid fierce, dry winds.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m07_004: I will wait here. Please, prove to me the extent of\nyour feelings!
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m08: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m08_001: Oh my, yes! Precisely the flower I asked for.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m08_002: Its beautiful color, its majestic form...and this one is\nlarger than most.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m08_003: You must have gone through much toil to find this\npiece of loveliness. Thank you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m08_004: But I am not yet satisfied. No! I have one additional,\nfinal request.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m09: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m09_001: All people are drawn to beauty. But true beauty often\nlies in places we cannot see.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m09_002: The jewels slumbering deep in the earth, honed to\nperfection, are a prime example.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m09_003: Would you please bring me an {Lowercase}Azure Heart{NormalCase}, a deep-\nblue gem clear as the sky?
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m09_004: Finding it will require a long, arduous journey...but\nam I not worth it?
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m010: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m010_001: Though many have professed their interest in me,\nnot one has fulfilled my requests.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m010_002: Until now. I am moved by your determination and\nthe depths of your desire!
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m010_003: I believe you would cherish me and see that I thrive!
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m010_004: Leilidahna—who you know as Leda—will forever\nremain my rival and my treasured ally.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m010_005: But I would not mind adding my beauty to your clan,\nand watching over her from outside.
MID_LGV_Scout_Oly_m010_006: Olympia Iris will join you—and you may behold my\ngraceful fighting from up close!
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m01_001: You'd like me to join you?
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m01_002: Huh? Join you?! No way I'd join forces with\nVritra's pet.
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m01_003: You've got a good eye! I have a better physique\nand sharper skills than most.
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m01_004: {SetColor=Gray}Hang on. He invited me first. I think I'll agree for\nnow, then I'll try to find out what's going on.{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m01_005: If you want my help so badly, then we should\nfight together!
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m01_006: O-OK. I guess if you want my help that badly, then\nI'll fight alongside you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m02_001: Yes! You hire me, and I'm gonna go wild!
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m02_002: Yeah! Now that we're all set, I'm gonna go wild!
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m02_003: No matter where I am, I'll always prove that I'm\nthe strongest!
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m03_001: Why'd you talk to me in the first place if you were\njust going to walk away?
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m04_001: You want me to join you? Is that because you heard\na rumor that I'm strong?
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m04_002: Um, I'm trying not to stand out too much. Sorry!\nCould you please go look somewhere else?
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m05_001: You want me to join? You know I'm Anatolia's\nguardian, yeah?
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m05_002: Join you? I'm Anatolia's guardian. I've got no urge to\nbe one of Vritra's minions.
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m05_003: Although, if I'm with you, maybe I can become\neven stronger than I am already.
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m05_004: I'm going to be the strongest ever! If I'm not strong,\nI haven't got any reason to exist.
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m05_005: Maybe it'd be good for me to have new experiences\nand try new kinds of training.
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m05_006: Yeah, OK. I'll lend you a hand if you can pay.\nI'll just tell the others I'm busy working.
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m06_001: Then it's settled! Together, I bet we can be the\nstrongest ever!
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m06_002: Can't there be two strongest people? Eh, whatever,\nI'm looking forward to working with you!
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m07: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m07_001: You're walking away after all?! Don't talk to me in\nthe first place if you're not interested!
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m08: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Naz_m08_001: What?! You don't have it! Why are you trying to\ndeceive me like that?
MID_LGV_Scout_Dai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Dai_m01_001: I've made up my mind. From now on, I'll fight\nalongside you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dai_m01_002: I've made up my mind. From now on, I'll fight\nalongside you.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dai_m01_003: Every one of the villagers thinks I'm a loser.\nEvery. Single. One.
MID_LGV_Scout_Dai_m01_004: I'm gonna get out of here for a bit. Once I'm gone,\nthey'll see how much they really need me!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dai_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Dai_m02_001: Whatever your reasons are, I'll fight with you. \nI'm gonna go on a rampage!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dai_m02_002: I dunno why I'm gonna fight with you, but I'm gonna\ndo it! I'm gonna go on a rampage!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dai_m02_003: They'll be begging me to come back!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dai_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_Scout_Dai_m03_001: You don't know how amazing I am, do you?! Don't\ncome crying to me later. You turned me down!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dai_m03_002: You don't know how amazing I am, do you?! Don't\ncome crying to me later. You turned me down!
MID_LGV_Scout_Dai_m04: <TH>
